# CAT3a: If a cardiac arrest and a respiratory arrest are both currently
# reported, they collectively convey a cardiorespiratory arrest.
#
# No ?alarm anchor, deliberately — this does not distinguish "the arriving
# alarm" from "an already-active one" the way CAT1b/CAT2a/an earlier
# version of this rule did. The two impliesClinicalEvent tags are independent
# facts: wherever each one currently sits (mda:Metric today; see
# ontology.ttl's "RECONSIDERED, REJECTED" note on why impliesClinicalEvent's
# domain stays mda:Metric, not mda:PhysiologicalProcess), this rule only
# asks whether the merged graph — background + situational + whatever the
# arriving alarm just contributed, exactly what assess.py already builds
# for every rule — currently contains both. No technical-pathway walk, no
# device/pathway scoping: two alarms conveying these on completely
# unrelated equipment still collectively convey a cardiorespiratory arrest.
#
# Because impliesClinicalEvent has zero persistence (situational-tagged, gone
# the instant its own alarm ends — see clinicalEvents.ttl's header), a
# match here means genuine temporal OVERLAP, not proximity: both
# conditions are being actively reported at this exact instant.
#
# Fires on EVERY arrival for as long as both conditions remain true, not
# just once at the moment they first coincide — assess.py has no per-rule
# state to suppress a repeat match, and this rule has no arrival-order
# anchor to make "first" a well-defined moment even if it tried. Collapsing
# repeat firings into one CardioRespiratoryArrest node per genuine episode
# is handled in mda_poc_assessment.py's minting step (deduplicated on the
# same (cardiacNode, respiratoryNode) pair), not here — keeping this query
# a pure, stateless "is it true right now" check.
#
# Validated against DATA/CAT_evaluation (cat3a_pos: Asystolie 08:00:00-
# 08:01:00 and Apneu 08:00:30-08:01:30, a genuine 30s overlap; cat3a_neg:
# Asystolie 08:00:00-08:00:20, Apneu arrives 08:00:40, no overlap; cat3c:
# same overlap as cat3a_pos with the arrival order swapped, confirming
# order genuinely does not matter now that there is no arrival anchor) —
# see cat_rules_report.md.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX clinicalEvent: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/clinical-event/>

SELECT ?cardiacNode ?respiratoryNode WHERE {
  ?cardiacNode mda:impliesClinicalEvent clinicalEvent:CardiacArrest .
  ?respiratoryNode mda:impliesClinicalEvent clinicalEvent:RespiratoryArrest .
}
